# Build outputs
#
# dist/ was tracked until 2026-09-10. Cloudflare Pages builds from source -
# the dashboard runs `npm run build` with output directory `dist` - so the
# committed copy was never what got deployed. What it did do was rewrite about
# 80 content-hashed chunk filenames on every build, so a one-line source change
# arrived as a 160-file diff of deletions and additions with the real change
# buried in it. PR #23 touched 184 files for ten small fixes.
#
# The gitignore entry used to be commented out "to allow dist for Cloudflare
# Worker". That worker is disabled (worker.js.disabled, wrangler.toml.disabled)
# and there are no GitHub workflows that consume dist/ either.
#
# `wrangler pages deploy` still works: it uploads the local dist/, which a
# local `npm run build` produces.
dist
dist-ssr
build
preview-dist
build-output.md

